2026-09-06T04:50:08.8094160Z    string which will be passed to String.format from Java code to replace each
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8114199Z    '%' occurrence with specific values.
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8143804Z 
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8154111Z    This lint warning checks for two related problems:
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8175457Z    (1) Formatting strings that are invalid, meaning that String.format will
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8202725Z    throw exceptions at runtime when attempting to use the format string.
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8224366Z    (2) Strings containing '%' that are not formatting strings getting passed
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8244227Z    to a String.format call. In this case the '%' will need to be escaped as
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8251306Z    '%%'.
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8251724Z 
2026-09-06T04:50:08.8253721Z    NOTE: Not all Strings which look like formatting strings are intended for
